<%# ONE DESKTOP DEVICE'S ROW, ON BOTH PAGES THAT LIST THEM (UX audit F6): your own Settings → Devices
    and an admin's view of another account (settings/users/edit). One partial, so the two show the
    same columns -- the day it was added, when it was last used -- and the same verb: Sign out, or
    Remove once it has expired, which is only tidying a row whose token is already refused.

    Locals: device, idle_limit (Device.idle_limit), url (the DELETE that signs it out), owner (nil on
    your own page; the account's email on an admin's page, which the confirmation names). %>
<% expired = device.expired?(idle_limit) %>
<% confirm =
     if expired then "Remove #{device.name} from this list?"
     elsif owner then "Sign #{device.name} out of #{owner}? It will need that account's password to sign in again."
     else "Sign out #{device.name}? It will need your password to sign in again."
     end %>
<li>
  <span class="settings-name"><%= device.name %></span>
  <% if expired %><span class="badge">Expired</span><% end %>
  <span class="settings-fact">added <%= time_at(device.created_at, style: :date) %></span>
  <span class="settings-fact"><% if device.last_seen_at %>used <%= time_at(device.last_seen_at, style: :relative) %><% else %>never used<% end %></span>
  <%= button_to expired ? "Remove" : "Sign out", url, method: :delete,
                class: "linkbtn danger small settings-remove",
                form: { data: { turbo_confirm: confirm } } %>
</li>
